def cable-input
  title "Input on a long lead: pull-up, series resistor and capacitor, TVS at the connector"
  about "A button, reed contact or open-collector sensor at the end of a long lead, read by an MCU input. A TVS at the
      connector takes ESD off the line; a 4.7 kΩ pull-up holds the line high against what the lead picks up; 1 kΩ in
      series and 100 nF to ground form a low-pass at the pin and limit the current into the pin's protection diodes
      while the TVS clamps (maker-coverage BL-12, HT-1, CK-16)."
  port in "the filtered signal – to the MCU input (one with a Schmitt trigger)"
  port vcc "the logic supply of that input (3.3 V; up to 5.0 V – the TVS's working voltage)"
  port gnd "ground – also the return wire of the lead"
  part J1 connector B2B-PH-K-S(LF)(SN) lcsc C131337 off_board "{as}: lead (JST PH, pin 1 = signal, pin 2 = GND)"
    notes "Its wires go to the button or sensor, not to another board of the project (off_board)."
  part D1 diode LESD5D5.0CT1G lcsc C5274290 "{as}: ESD protection at the connector (TVS 5 V)"
    notes "Bidirectional; next to J1, its ground pad short to J1's ground pin."
  part R1 resistor 0805W8F4701T5E lcsc C17673 value 4.7k "{as}: pull-up 4.7 k"
  part R2 resistor 0805W8F1001T5E lcsc C17513 value 1k "{as}: series 1 k"
  part C1 capacitor CC0805KRX7R9BB104 lcsc C49678 value 100nF "{as}: filter 100 nF"
  net line @vcc J1.1 D1.cathode R1.2 R2.1
    notes "The wire side: connector, TVS, pull-up."
  net in @vcc R2.2 C1.1
  net vcc R1.1
  net gnd J1.2 D1.anode C1.2
  covers REQ.missing/leave HINT.cable_line HINT.esd HINT.debounce LVL.undefined LIM.v
  notes "Pull-up 4.7 kΩ: a design choice inside the '10 kΩ or less' for inputs on long leads (HINT.cable_line,
      maker-coverage HT-1) – about 0.7 mA through the contact at 3.3 V. It sits on the wire side, so the contact
      current does not flow through R2."
  notes "Series 1 kΩ: between the TVS and the pin. While the TVS clamps (VC 11.6 V at 5 A, 8/20 µs – LRC
      LESD5D5.0CT1G, p. 2) it keeps the current into the pin's protection diodes near 8 mA for those microseconds; it
      is the series resistance REQ.missing/leave asks for (CK-16; the emonTx uses 1 kΩ and a TVS)."
  notes "100 nF with R2: the falling edge (contact closes) with τ = 1 kΩ × 100 nF = 0.1 ms, the rising edge with (4.7
      k + 1 k) × 100 nF = 0.57 ms. It removes spikes, not contact bounce (milliseconds): debounce in the firmware
      (HINT.debounce). For pulses faster than about 1 kHz (flow sensor, anemometer) a smaller capacitor."
  notes "The RC makes slow edges: read it with an input that has a Schmitt trigger enabled; a plain CMOS input may
      toggle several times while the edge passes its threshold."
  notes "TVS LESD5D5.0CT1G: working voltage 5.0 V, leakage ≤ 1 µA at 5.0 V – less than 5 mV across the pull-up. On a 5
      V rail that reaches 5.25–5.5 V the working voltage is exceeded (LIM.v holds a TVS to VRWM without margin): take
      a TVS with VRWM ≥ 5.5 V there. It is bidirectional; its SPICE model is one junction, right while the line stays
      between 0 V and VCC."
  notes "J1 is marked off_board: REQ.missing/leave then checks that a resistor stands between the wire and the MCU
      pin. For a lead to another board of the project, model it as a cable in the graph instead – HINT.cable_line
      names its net."
  notes "A sensor that needs a supply wants a third wire and its own feed (and a fuse or resistor in it) – not in this
      block."
  notes "sim.json: the in net under the MCU's inputs. The contact is off the board and not simulated; closed, the line
      and the input sit at 0 V and the pull-up carries the 0.7 mA."
  set test {
     "connect": {
      "in": "SIG",
      "vcc": "3V3"
     },
     "sim": {
      "mcu": {
       "U1": {
        "outputs": [
         "LED_SDI",
         "LED_CLK",
         "LED_LE",
         "LED_OE"
        ],
        "inputs": [
         "SIG"
        ],
        "pullups": [
         "BTN"
        ],
        "pullup_ohm": 50000
       }
      }
     }
     }
